<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13436"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 12:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->1&#41; Fled the scene. During Vian murder, Denny was interupted by phone ringing &#40;by his own admission&#41; and thus fled the scene before harming the children because...he knew that what he was doing was wrong. During the murder of Katherine Bright, panicked when Kevin freed himself and jumped him. Shot Kevin &#40;leaving him for dead&#41; and then had to quickly stab Katherine &#40;rather than strangling her&#41; to leave no witnesses when Kevin managed to escape. Fled the scene because...he knew he was committing a crime. <BR> <BR>2&#41; Kept momentos of each crime to have rememberances of the experience &#34;for everyday use&#34;. He was aware, during the crime, that he was doing something that he would want to do all of the time, but would not be able to...because it was against the law. <BR> <BR>3&#41;Wrote letters &#40;either the &#39;BTK Denny&#39; who committed the crime, or the &#34;church Denny&#34; who was obviously aware of &#34;BTK Denny&#34;&#41; to the police to taunt them because...he knew they were looking for him because he was a criminal. <BR> <BR>4&#41;In the context of one of the letters noted that he was aware of what he was doing but tried to blame it on &#34;factor x&#34; and a &#34;monster&#34;. He noted that he was aware that the public would view him as a &#34;psychotic personality with sexual perversion&#34;. He knew he should seek &#34;psychiatric help&#34; but claimed he didn&#39;t for fear of ridicule. <BR>He went so far as to say that it was &#34;too bad that society must suffer&#34;, thereby acertaining not only that he was aware that his behavior was psychologically abnormal, but that he also realized the far-reaching effect on society as a whole &#40;note that he did not limit the suffering to his victims&#41;. <BR> <BR>5&#41; He stalked his victims. He admitted to &#34;taking down numbers&#34; and &#34;waiting, waiting&#34; &#40;or at least, the &#34;monster&#34; did&#41; which shows premeditation. <BR> <BR>6&#41; As time went on, he began to choose weaker, older, more predictable &#40;or so he thought&#41; victims. During his known killings there were several problems which caused him to deviate from his intended itenerary. He changed his M.O. to compensate. This shows that he was aware of continuity and &#39;learned&#39; as he went, thus showing that these were not 10 isolated incidents. <BR> <BR>7&#41; &#34;Will there be more?&#34;. Again, shows premeditation. <BR> <BR>If using DID as a basis for an insanity plea requires that Denny prove that he was unaware at the time of the murder that what he was doing was wrong, or that &#34;host Denny&#34; was not aware of what &#34;BTK Denny&#34; was up to, he might have problems. The seven examples above are gleaned from the evidence known to the general public. The DA has indicated that they have a substantial amount of evidence that the public is unaware of. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13436-->
<!--Post: 13457--><!--Time: 1115340608-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13457"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 5:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why am I talking DID? <BR> <BR>Because there is no other form of the insanity defense that would survive the TONS of evidence that BTK knew his conduct was wrong. <BR> <BR>For an insanity defense to work in this case, the defendant has to prove two contradictory facts: 1&#41; &#42;I&#42; didn&#39;t do it, and 2&#41; &#42;I&#42; was insane when &#42;I&#42; did it.   <BR> <BR>The ONLY form of insanity that fits is DID, because it is the ONLY mental disease that splits the &#34;I&#34; and allows both statements to be true. <BR> <BR>Phoenix <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13457-->
<!--Post: 13459--><!--Time: 1115341739-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13459"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 6:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point Professor, so where is the case law for the jurisdiction of Kansas to use this DID defense? Again, the case law you cited above doesn&#39;t reference anything close to Kansas.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13459-->
<!--Post: 13474--><!--Time: 1115357787-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13474"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 10:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hang &#39;em both and let God sort &#39;em out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13474-->
<!--Post: 13475--><!--Time: 1115361132-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13475"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 11:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky: <BR> <BR>There is no case law on point in Kansas. <BR> <BR>If the defense has a psychologist who will testify that there is a DID alter, the one who confessed, and killed, and saved trophies, but it wasn&#39;t the Dennis Rader alter, this case goes to a jury on every count. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s the rub--- prove him sane <BR> <BR> <BR>or he walks. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13475-->
<!--Post: 13476--><!--Time: 1115362747-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13476"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 11:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky: <BR> <BR>Sorry, it&#39;s late and I got way more flip than the question deserved. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s how it works... <BR> <BR>1. The defense provides a mental disease/defect, which will prevent a person from distinguishing right from wrong. <BR> <BR>2.  They find a Doctor/Psychologist who makes a Dx of that disease/defect. <BR> <BR>3.  That witness testifies that BTK is an alter of DR; that BTK knows his conduct is wrong, but DR does not control the BTK alter, and while in that state can&#39;t distinguish right from wrong.  <BR> <BR>4.  Now the prosecution evidence, while still relevant, is much less effective.  The evidence of the multiple personalities lies with the people who knew DR during those periods, and they all say he was good father/church member etc.  A decent defense attorney could use them as evidence of a good alter setting up a Jeckel/Hyde DID defense. <BR> <BR>That approach makes the DA have to prove that the DR &#40;who was elected whatever in his church&#41; and BTK are the same personality. <BR> <BR>Plus the 10 homicide cases. <BR> <BR>Bottom Line: as a tactic it makes the DA fight on defense ground.  Always better for the defense. <BR> <BR> <BR>And Rocky, good defense lawyers know it&#39;s easier to make new law in a case than new facts. <BR> <BR>Phoenix <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13476-->
<!--Post: 13480--><!--Time: 1115379240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13480"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 4:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s what I was affraid you were going to say! You know I&#39;m thinking that because DR used the church computer to manifest correspondence by BTK the DA could challenge that disease/defect/DID theory. <BR> <BR>Yea, but you got to have grounds for an appeal and there is no case law to review for the DID. I hope Judge Waller is sharp as a tack. This will come down to a battle of the experts! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13480-->
<!--Post: 13484--><!--Time: 1115384453-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 6:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->man, my hand has been up all day, and he still hasnt called on me <BR> <BR>Professor P, I have a question!!  Over here, call on me!! <BR> <BR>Question: Since rader is being so helpful to his defense team, when the state turns over the evidence, is rader actually going to be able to see and handle the evidence? If its true, it makes me sicker than sick. <BR> <BR>Not only would that entail seeing all the police reports, and in a sense &#34;spying&#34; in on everything that the cops have been up to for 30 years,  <BR>Im bothered that he will be able to handle the physical evidence, even if its in plastic bags. <BR>Can you imagine how much of a reward its gonna be for him to hold the ropes, pics, pj&#39;s, letters he sent.... <BR> <BR>This is not right, if true.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13484-->
<!--Post: 13487--><!--Time: 1115394412-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13487"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 8:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Prof and Rocky....I KNEW this was probably going to head the way of insanity... <BR>Prof:  Thank you for making it easier for us lay-people citizens of Wichita to understand <BR>Rocky: Thank you also for your input and insight...the emotional ties you have bring out such good questions and points. <BR>I just hope Nola and Judge W. are forseeing all of this also, <BR>I like the diskette idea...how can he possibly say the &#34;dark&#34; side did things unbeknownst to the &#34;good&#34; side when a MAJOR piece of evidence came the the &#34;good&#34; side. <BR>The demon @&#42;&#42; sares me. <BR>OMG - IF HE WALKS&#62;&#62;&#62;&#62; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13487-->
<!--Post: 13501--><!--Time: 1115403717-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13501"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty: <BR> <BR>The defendant has a right to see the evidence.  Copies of reports and photographs are usually provided to the defendant, but that&#39;s probably unworkable here.  To go to trial without showing Rader all the reports and photos would invite an ineffective assistance of counsel claim that might reverse a conviction. <BR> <BR>Physical evidence is a different matter.  He gets to see it, but not necessarily touch it, and not in private.  It&#39;s usually done in open court. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13501-->
<!--Post: 13505--><!--Time: 1115406407-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13505"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 12:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is so great...it&#39;s like we get to know and understand all the play by play action on this thing.... <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13505-->
<!--Post: 13511--><!--Time: 1115432027-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13511"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bluepup<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bluepup<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 7:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Phoenix, I have a question for you.  <BR>Some time ago I heard &#40;either read an article or saw on TV&#41; something about some states trying to change their insanity pleas..instead of the plea being &#34;Not Guilty by reason of Insanity&#34; they wanted to change it to &#34;GUILTY by reason of Insanity&#34;. To your knowledge, has this been done anywhere &#40;or in Kansas&#41; yet?   <BR>It sounds like a good idea to me...but curious what others may think of the idea.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13511-->
<!--Post: 13518--><!--Time: 1115440332-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13518"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 9:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bluepup: <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll check on other states/jurisdictions, but in Kansas the answer is no. <BR> <BR>The reason is that &#42;guilt&#42; means that the act was done by the defendant, AND the defendant knew the act was wrong &#40;criminal intent.&#41;  If there is no criminal intent there is no guilt.  The presence of legal insanity, by definition, negates criminal intent. <BR> <BR>Insanity defenses are part of a class of defenses that focus on the lack of criminal intent such as intoxication, etc. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13518-->
<!--Post: 13530--><!--Time: 1115516960-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13530"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bluepup<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bluepup<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 07, 2005 - 6:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Phoenix.  <BR>I think the &#40;legal&#41; definition of insanity was the crux of the problem they were trying to solve by changing the plea.  <BR>After trials, jurors were saying they believed that defendants were &#34;insane&#34; BUT they also believed the defendants knew that what they were doing was wrong.  <BR> <BR>I can kinda see where they were coming from, especially in this case. I believe DTDC knew it was wrong &#40;criminal intent&#41; but I also don&#39;t think he is sane, because would anyone sane do what he did?  <BR>But then again, my definition of insane is not a legal definition.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13530-->
